---
title: Capabilities and execution modes
description: Exact permission names, native-host grants and actionable preview.2 diagnostics.
sidebar:
  order: 7
---

A service name is not a permission token. `HttpService` needs `network.client`;
`HttpServerService` needs `network.server`. Declare exact, case-sensitive tokens
in the manifest, and request only what the app uses.

| Token | Operation and required provider |
| --- | --- |
| `network.client` | Outbound HTTP/HTTPS; a supported transport and destination policy. |
| `network.server` | Hosted HTTP; a supported transport and binding policy. |
| `network.raw` | Raw TCP/UDP, together with its client/server direction grant. |
| `Clipboard` | ClipboardService with the host clipboard adapter. |
| `Dialogs` | File picking with a supported adapter; a picked path is not unrestricted file access. |
| `Storage` | App-private storage with a host-installed scope and `Storage.ApplicationId`. |
| `Notifications` / `Tray` | The selected Windows shell adapter; GTK reports unsupported. |
| `HostServices` | Explicitly registered host bindings and their separate service grants. |
| `NativeExtensions` | Declared, trusted native loading with explicit host approval. |

The app requests capabilities; the host grants them. A manifest cannot install a
missing provider or override platform policy. HTTP does not need `network.raw`.

Check Types analyzes declared Development sources without executing them.
Restricted static checking remains unsupported. **Run App** exercises supported
native-host grants. **Inspect Layout** executes a separate unprivileged generation
and refuses privileged capabilities and native extensions. Native extensions
require an explicitly approved host launch with `--allow-native`; editor Run App
does not request that approval.

## When the app will not start

Save source, check types and read **LUI Preview** Output. Preview.2 preserves fixed
missing-capability and startup reasons without arbitrary native stderr or private
source. A callback failure can leave the window open while the operation fails.
Keep the SDK and project pin matched. Do not remove a required grant just to use
the inspector. Try the [complete HTTP project](../recipes/#local-http-client-and-server).
